$DATUM Ethyl
(2E,5S,7R,9E,11E)-5,7-bis(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)-13-(4-methoxybenzyloxy)trideca-2,9,11-trienoate
(8b). LiCl (60 mg, 1.41 mmol, 1.3 equiv) was heated 1 min with a heatgun
and slowly cooled to rt under argon. The flask was then cooled to 0 °C
and aldehyde 8a (612 mg, 1.09 mmol, 1 equiv) in MeCN (11 mL) was added.
Triethyl phosphonoacetate (259 μL, 1.31 mmol, 1.2 equiv) was added
dropwise and the mixture was stirred for 5 min before adding DBU (195 μL,
1.31 mmol, 1.2 equiv). The orange mixture was allowed to warm up to rt
and stirred for 20 h. The mixture was diluted with Et2O (50 mL) and
washed with a saturated aqueous solution of NH4Cl (2 × 50 mL) and brine
(50 mL). The organic phases were dried over MgSO4, filtered and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude material was purified by
flash chromatography on silica gel (petroleum ether/EtOAc = 95:5). Ester
8b (585 mg, 0.924 mmol, 85%, dr > 98:2) as a colorless oil. Formula:
C35H60O6Si2; Molecular weight: 633.03 g.mol-1; [α]D 20 -16.8 (c 1.10,
CHCl3). IR (neat): 2953, 2929, 2856, 1720, 1513, 1463, 1363, 1249, 1086,
1039, 989 cm-1. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.27 (m, 2H), 6.94 (m, 1H),
6.88 (m, 2H), 6.21 (dd, J = 15.2, J = 10.4 Hz, 1H), 6.05 (dd, J = 15.1, J
= 10.6 Hz, 1H), 5.82 (d, J = 15.7 Hz, 1H), 5.73-5.59 (m, 2H), 4.44 (s,
2H), 4.22-4.13 (m, 2H), 4.02 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 2H), 3.90 (m, 1H), 3.80 (s,
3H), 3.78 (m, 1H), 2.45-2.15 (m, 4H), 1.70-1.51 (m, 2H), 1.27 (t, J = 7.1
Hz, 3H), 0.88 (br s, 18H), 0.04 (br s, 12H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
166.3 (s), 159.2 (s), 145.7 (d), 133.0 (d), 132.1 (d), 130.7 (d), 130.4
(s), 129.4 (d, 2C), 127.8 (d), 123.5 (d), 113.8 (d, 2C), 71.6 (t), 70.2
(t), 69.1 (d), 68.5 (d), 60.2 (t), 55.3 (q), 44.7 (t), 40.8 (t), 40.1
(t), 25.9 (q, 3C), 25.8 (q, 3C), 18.0 (s, 2C), 14.3 (q), -4.2 (q), -4.45
(q), -4.49 (q, 2C). HRMS: calculated for C35H60O6NaSi2 (M+Na+): 655.3821.
Found: 655.3822.
