$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM δ-Sanshool, Compounds 20 and 21; General Procedure A solution of the
appropriate phosphonate 6, 18, or 19 (0.4 mmol) in THF (1 mL) was added
to a suspension of LiOH (34 mg, 0.8 mmol) in dry THF (5 mL) in the
presence of 4 Å molecular sieves. After 20 min, a solution of aldehyde 17
(30 mg, 0.2 mmol) in THF (1 mL) was added and the reaction mixture was
heated at reflux temperature for 3 h. After cooling, the mixture was
filtered and evaporated to dryness. The crude residue was purified by
column chromatography (CH2Cl2-MeOH, 98:2). δ-Sanshool Yield: 46 mg (85%)
(eluent: PE-EtOAc, 7:3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, molecular sieves used, alternative preparation shown,
14% overall yield in four steps starting from diethyl
(2E,4E)-2,4-hexadienylphosphonate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Total Synthesis of δ-Sanshool and Analogues Thereof
